From 992b59d2c5c2244caeb317a617c45216bac02d34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:14:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: novatek-nt36536: use HS for Y900 DVT2 shutdown

The active BOE DVT2 stock panel describes its off command set as
qcom,mdss-dsi-off-command-state = "dsi_hs_mode", while initialization
uses LP mode. The current driver leaves MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM enabled for
both sequences, so the MIPI DSI core sets USE_LPM on the shutdown packets.

Clear MODE_LPM only around this panel variant's display-off and enter-sleep
commands, then restore the exact original flags even on a transfer error.
The bonded MSM manager passes the same message flags to both links.
Keep the existing commands, delays, initialization and other variants.

This corrects a stock-protocol mismatch; it does not yet establish that
physical wake is repaired. CI51 still renders desktop screenshots after
wake while its physical panel stays dark. The display-bus diagnostics
remain enabled for the next bounded test, not for production promotion.

Protocol interpretation follows Lenovo's pinned dsi_panel_tx_cmd_set():
https://github.com/lenovo-basements/android_kernel_lenovo_sm8750-modules/blob/e1f324632d70b2427751820cd48eefc45baab0ce/qcom/opensource/display-drivers/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c
Board transfer modes were verified against this tablet's runtime DT.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@localhost>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c
index 402e2265516b..97209e112bc2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c
@@ -392,10 +392,16 @@ static int y900_boe_nt36536e_init_seq(struct mipi_dsi_multi_context *dsi_ctx)
 
 static int y900_boe_nt36536e_exit_seq(struct mipi_dsi_multi_context *dsi_ctx)
 {
+	struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi = dsi_ctx->dsi;
+	unsigned long mode_flags = dsi->mode_flags;
+
+	/* The BOE DVT2 panel's shutdown sequence uses high-speed commands. */
+	dsi->mode_flags &= ~MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_off_multi(dsi_ctx);
 	mipi_dsi_msleep(dsi_ctx, 20);
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_enter_sleep_mode_multi(dsi_ctx);
 	mipi_dsi_msleep(dsi_ctx, 120);
+	dsi->mode_flags = mode_flags;
 
 	return dsi_ctx->accum_err;
 }
